#block(above: 1.05em, below: 0.42em)[#text(size: 13pt, weight: "bold")[Proverbs and sayings]]
#block(above: 0.42em, below: 0.5em)[
+ Ako ih ne možeš pobijediti, pridruži im se - if you can’t beat them, join them
+ Ako već radiš, radi kako treba - if you’re doing something, do it properly\/if a job is worth doing, it’s worth doing well
+ Bez alata nema zanata - without tools there’s no craft\/using the right tool for the job
+ Bez dlake na jeziku - without a \[single\] hair on the tongue\/without mincing ones words or saying too much
+ Bez muke nema nauke - without suffering there\'s no learning\/no pain no gain
+ Bogu iza nogu - behind God\'s legs\/in the middle of nowhere
+ Bolje grob nego rob - better grave than slave\/it’s better to die on one’s feet than live on one’s knees
+ Bolje ikad nego nikad - better ever than never\/better late than never
+ Bolje išta nego ništa - better something than nothing\/something is better than nothing
+ Bolje spriječiti nego liječiti - better to prevent than to cure\/better safe than sorry
+ Bolje vrabac u ruci, nego golub na grani - better a sparrow in the hand, than a pigeon on the branch\/a bird in the hand is worth two in the bush
+ Brigo moja prijeđi na drugoga - \[ou\] my worry, pass onto someone else\/referring to shirking of responsibility\/passing the buck
+ Čist račun, duga ljubav - clean bill, long-lasting love\/short reckonings make long friends
+ Čistoća je pola zdravlja - cleanliness is half the health\/cleanliness is next to godliness
+ Čovjek je čovjeku vuk - a man is wolf to man\/homo homini lupus\/used for situations where people behave in a way comparable to a wolf\/dog eat dog
+ Čovjek uči dok je živ - a man learns as long as he lives\/live and learn
+ Danas jesmo, sutra nismo - today we are, tomorrow we’re not\/here today and gone tomorrow
+ Daleko od očiju, daleko od srca - far from eyes, far from heart\/out of sight, out of mind
+ Daš mu prst, a on uzme cijelu ruku - give him a finger and he takes the whole arm\/give him an inch and he’ll take a mile
+ Dobra vijest se brzo širi, a loša još brže - good news travels fast and bad even faster\/bad news travels fast
+ Doč će maca na vratanca - the kitty will come to the little door\/you’ll get your just deserts eventually
+ Drži vodu dok majstori ne odu - holds water until the repairmen leave\/referring to a low quality job or solution
+ Gdje ima dima ima i vatre - where there\'s smoke, there\'s fire
+ Gdje si bio? Nigdje. Što si radio? Ništa. - where were you? nowhere. what did you do? nothing.\/time-wasting
+ Gledati kao tele u šarena vrata - looking like a calf at a colourful door\/like a deer in headlights
+ I zidovi imaju uši - walls have ears
+ Igla u plastu sijena - needle in a haystack
+ Imati glavu u oblacima - \[to have ones\] head in the clouds
+ Imati veče oči od želuca - eyes bigger than the stomach
+ Ispeci, pa reci - bake it, then say it\/think before you speak
+ Jabuka ne pada daleko od stabla - the apple doesn\'t fall far from the tree
+ Jedna lasta ne čini proljeće - one swallow doesn\'t make it spring\/one bird doesn\'t make a summer
+ Jednom smrkne, drugom svane - as it goes dark for one, it dawns for another\/one man’s loss is another man’s gain
+ Kad čeljad nije bijesna, ni kuća nije tijesna - when children aren’t furious, the house isn’t too small either\/if people are reasonable, solutions can be found
+ Kad mačka ode, miševi kolo vode - when the cat\'s away, the mice dance kolo \[traditional circle dance\]\/while the cat\'s away the mice will play
+ Kad na vrbi rodi grožđe - when a willow bears grapes\/when pigs fly
+ Kad stvari krenu nizbrdo - when things start going downhill\/when it rains, it pours
+ Kak pri jelu, tak pri djelu - as while eating, so while working\/the way one behaves at mealtime is the way one behaves at worktime
+ Kakav otac, takav sin - like father, like son
+ Kako došlo, tako prošlo - as it came, so it went\/easy come, easy go
+ Kao da su mu sve lađe potonule - like all his ships have sunk\/looking depressed
+ Kao muha bez glave - like a fly without the head\/like a headless chicken
+ Kap koja je prelila čašu - the drop that made the glass overflow\/the last straw\/the straw that broke the camel’s back
+ Klin se klinom izbija - a wedge is removed by a wedge\/fight fire with fire
+ Ko te šiša?! - who cuts your hair?!\/nobody cares \[about you\/what you have to say\]\/stuff you
+ Koliko para, toliko muzike - how much money, that much music\/you get what you pay for
+ Kom opanci, kom obojci - peasant or soldier footwear of old\/you get what you get\/whatever happens, happens
+ Krv nije voda - blood is not water\/blood is thicker than water
+ Kućni prag je najveća planina - the home doorstep is the biggest mountain\/first step is always the hardest
+ Kud puklo da puklo\/Šta bude da bude - where it breaks, let it break\/whatever happens, happens
+ Kud svi Turci, tu i ćoravi Mujo - where all Turks go, so does the blind Mujo\/to blindly follow\/when in Rome, do as the Romans do
+ Lako je biti general poslije bitke - it’s easy to be a general after the battle\/it’s easy to be wise after the event
+ Lakše je reći nego učiniti - it’s easier to say than to do\/easier said than done
+ Lezi lebe da te jedem - serbian saying: lie down bread so that I may eat you\/regarding laziness
+ Lijep\(a\) kao slika - pretty as a picture
+ Mi o vuku, a vuk na vrata - we \[talk\] about the wolf and the wolf \[comes\] to the door\/talk of the devil, and the devil appears\/speak of the devil
+ Mladost – ludost - youthfulness – craziness\/youth is reckless
+ Mlatiti praznu slamu - beating empty hay\/flogging a dead horse
+ Motati oko malog prsta - wrapping around the little finger
+ Motati se kao mačka oko vruče kaše - circling like a cat around hot porridge
+ Na jedno uho unutra, na drugo van - in one ear and out the other
+ Na muci se poznaju junaci - during suffering you identify the heroes\/when the going gets tough, the tough get going
+ Ne diraj lava dok spava - don’t touch a lion while it sleeps\/let sleeping dogs lie
+ Ne laje pas zbog sela - dog doesn\'t bark because of the village\/sounding off due to own self-interest
+ Ne možeš imati i ovce i novce - you can’t have both the sheep and the money\/you can’t have your cake and eat it too
+ Ne možeš ništa na brzinu - you can’t rush anything\/Rome wasn’t built in a day
+ Ne možeš svima ugoditi - you can’t please everyone
+ Ne niči gdje te ne siju - don\'t sprout where you\'re not planted\/don\'t stick your nose where it doesn\'t belong
+ Ne traži dlaku u jajetu - don\'t look for a hair in the egg\/don\'t be so nitpicky
+ Ne trči pred rudo - don\'t run in front of the carriage\/don\'t jump the gun
+ Ne valja se s rogatim bosti - it\'s no good to \[text cut off in source — the saying means roughly \"don\'t pick a fight with someone tougher than you \/ don\'t butt heads with the one who has horns\"\] \(check?#degmark \)
+ Ne zna se tko je lud, a tko blesav - It\'s unknown who\'s crazy and who\'s foolish.
+ Ne zna se tko pije, a tko plaća - It\'s unknown who\'s drinking and who\'s paying.
+ Neće grom u koprive - Lightning won\'t strike into stinging nettle.
+ Nema kruha bez motike - There\'s no bread without the shovel \(As you sow, so shall you reap\).
+ Nema odmora dok traje obnova - There\'s no rest while the renovations go on \(There\'s no rest for the wicked\).
+ Nema teorije \/ Nema šanse - There’s no theory \/ There’s no chance.
+ Nesreća nikad ne dolazi sama - Misfortune never comes alone \(When it rains, it pours\).
+ Ni mrava ne bi zgazio - Wouldn\'t even trample an ant \(Wouldn\'t hurt a fly\).
+ Nije gotovo dok nije gotovo - It ain’t over till it’s over.
+ Nije se još rodio koji bi svakom ugodio - None were yet born that could please everyone \(You can\'t please everyone\).
+ Nije svaki dan nedjelja \/ Nije svaki dan Božić - Not every day is Sunday \/ Not every day is Christmas \(Christmas comes but once a year\).
+ Nije život med i mlijeko - Life isn’t honey and milk \(Life isn’t just a bowl of cherries\).
+ Nikad ne reci nikad - Never say never.
+ Novac kvari ljude - Money corrupts people.
+ Odijelo ne čini čovjeka - A suit does not make a man \(Don’t judge a book by its cover\).
+ O tom – potom - About it – eventually \(We’ll cross that bridge when we come to it\).
+ Obećanje ludom radovanje - A promise makes a fool happy \(Don\'t be fooled by empty promises \/ There’s no such thing as a free lunch\).
+ Od viška glava ne boli - Surplus doesn\'t make the head hurt \(Better more than less\).
+ Pametniji popušta - The smarter one yields \(You conquer by yielding\).
+ Pametnom je dosta jednom reči - It’s enough to say it once to a smart person \(A word to the wise \[is enough\]\).
+ Pas koji laje, ne grize - A barking dog doesn\'t bite \(Barking dogs seldom bite\).
+ Poklonjenom konju se ne gleda u zube - Don\'t look a gift horse in the mouth.
+ Pomozi si sam i Bog će ti pomoći - Help yourself and God will help you \(God helps those that help themselves\).
+ Pored takvih prijatelja, što će mi neprijatelji - With friends like these, who needs enemies.
+ Poslije kiše dolazi sunce \/ Svjetlo je uvijek na kraju tunela - After the rain comes the sun \/ There’s always light at the end of a tunnel.
+ Postoji vrijeme i mjesto za sve - There’s a time and place for everything.
+ Praviti slona od muhe \/ Od komarca napraviti magarca - Making an elephant out of an ant \/ To make a donkey out of a mosquito \(To make a mountain out of a molehill\).
+ Prebit ću te kao vola u kupusu - I\'ll beat you like \[beating\] an ox in a cabbage \[field\] \(You are in big trouble\).
+ Prelijevati iz šupljeg u prazno - To pour from hollow into empty \(Robbing Peter to pay Paul\).
+ Prevesti kao žednog preko vode - To lead someone like leading a thirsty across the water \(To trick someone badly\).
+ Prošla baba s kolačima - Old woman with the cookies went by \(To miss the boat\).
+ Prvo skoči, pa reci \'hop\' - Leap first and then say \'jump\' \(Look before you leap\).
+ Puna šaka brade - A fistful of beard \(Very satisfied about something\).
+ Puno baba, kilavo dijete - Many midwives \[make a\] lazy child \(Too many cooks spoil the broth\).
+ Riba ribi grize rep \/ Petar Petru plete petlju - One fish bites another fish’s tail \/ Peter knits a knot for Peter \(Popular tongue twisters for children\).
+ Riječi ti se pozlatile - May your words become gold plated \(I very much wish for it to be as you said\).
+ Rugala se sova sjenici - The owl mocked the tit \(Pot calling the kettle black\).
+ Ruka ruku mije - One hand washes another \(Scratching each other’s back\).
+ Sigurno je sigurno - What’s sure is sure \(Stick with the tried and tested \/ Better safe than sorry\).
+ Sreća u nesreći - Good luck in bad luck \(Something good occurs following on from something bad \/ A blessing in disguise\).
+ Sto ljudi, sto ćudi - Hundred people, hundred personalities \(Different strokes for different folks\).
+ Sutra je novi dan \/ Nije sve propalo - Tomorrow is another day \/ Not all is lost.
+ Svaka medalja ima dvije strane - Every medal has two sides \(There are two sides to every coin\).
+ Svaka ptica svom jatu leti - Every bird flies to its own flock \(Birds of a feather stick together\).
+ Svako zlo za neko dobro - Every evil for some good \(Every cloud has a silver lining\).
+ Svakog gosta tri dana dosta - Every guest becomes a burden after 3 days \(Fish and visitors stink after 3 days\).
+ Svakom loncu poklopac - Being a lid for every pot \(Always having something to add \/ Having to have the last word\).
+ Sve je dobro što se dobro svrši - All is well that ends well.
+ Sve se može kad se hoće - All can be done when it’s willed \(Where there’s a will, there’s a way\).
+ Sve se vraća, sve se plaća - Everything gets returned, everything gets paid \(What goes around, comes around\).
+ Sve što je lijepo, kratko traje - All that’s nice, lasts short \(All good things must come to an end \/ Time flies when having fun\).
+ Sve u svoje vrijeme - All in its own time \(All in due time\).
+ Svi putevi vode u Rim - All roads lead to Rome.
+ Svuda je lijepo, ali doma je najljepše - It’s nice everywhere, but it’s nicest at home \(East or west, home is best\).
+ Štedi za crne dane - Save for dark days \(Save for a rainy day\).
+ Što je, je - What is, is \(Give credit where it’s due\).
+ Što je bilo, bilo je - What was, was \(Let bygones be bygones\).
+ Što je, tu je - What is, here it is \(It is what it is \/ What can’t be cured, must be endured \/ Playing the hand one is dealt\).
+ Što možeš danas, ne ostavljaj za sutra - What you can do today, don\'t leave for tomorrow.
+ Što se babi htilo, to se babi snilo - What the old woman wanted, she imagined \(When wishes shape convictions\).
+ Što više, to bolje - The more the merrier.
+ Šutnja je zlato \/ Tišina je zlatna \/ Šutnja zlata vrijedi - Silence is gold \/ Quietness is golden \/ Silence is worth gold \(Silence is golden\).
+ Teško žabu u vodu natjerati - Hard to get a frog into the water \(Didn\'t take much persuading\).
+ Tiha voda brege dere - Silent water carves hills \(Silent water runs deep\).
+ Tko čeka, taj dočeka - Who waits, gets \(Good things come to those who wait\).
+ Tko jači, taj kvači - The one who’s stronger, clutches \(Might is right \/ Stronger prevails\).
+ Tko ne riskira, taj ne profitira - Who doesn\'t risk, doesn\'t profit \(Nothing ventured, nothing gained\).
+ Tko pita, taj ne skita - The one who asks, doesn’t stray \(The only stupid question is the one that’s not asked\).
+ Tko pod drugim jamu kopa, sam u nju pada - The one that digs a hole for another, falls in it himself.
+ Tko prvi, njegova djevojka - Who’s first, gets the girl \(First come, first served\).
+ Tko radi, ne boji se gladi - Who works, doesn’t fear hunger \(Those that are not lazy don’t worry about not having enough to survive\).
+ Tko radi, taj i griješi - Who works, makes mistakes \(If you don’t make mistakes, you don’t make anything\).
+ Tko rano rani, dvije sreće grabi - Who earlies early, grabs twice the luck \(The early bird catches the worm\).
+ Tko se jednom opeče, puše i na hladno - Who gets burned once, blows even when it’s cold \(Once bitten, twice shy\).
+ Tko se zadnji smije, najslađe se smije - Who laughs last, laughs the sweetest \(He who laughs last, laughs best\).
+ Tko uči znat će, tko štedi imat će - Who studies will know, who saves will have.
+ Tko umije, njemu dvije - The one who is able, receives twice.
+ Tko visoko leti, nisko pada - Who flies high, falls low \(The bigger they are, the harder they fall\).
+ Tko zna bolje, široko mu polje - Who knows better, his field is wide \(If someone thinks they know better, best of luck to them\).
+ Tko zna, zna - Who knows, knows \(When complimenting advanced knowledge or skill\).
+ To je mačji kašalj - That’s a cat’s cough \(It’s a piece of cake\).
+ Trbuhom za kruhom - \[With\] belly chasing bread \(Leaving in search of a better life\).
+ Tresla se brda, rodio se miš \/ Mnogo buke ni zbog čega - Hills shook, a mouse was born \/ Much ado about nothing.
+ Trla baba lan, da joj prođe dan - Old woman grinded flax \[seeds\] to pass the time \(Wasting time\).
+ U laži su kratke noge - While lying, your legs are short \(If you lie you won\'t get far\).
+ U nevolji se poznaje prijatelj - In hardship a friend is known \(A friend in need is a friend indeed\).
+ U svakoj šali ima pola istine - Every joke is half true \(Many a true word is spoken in jest\).
+ U tom grmu leži zec - In that bush lies the rabbit \(Therein lies the rub\).
+ Umiljato janje dvije majke siše - A cuddly lamb suckles two mothers \(Being nice will gain you more benefits\).
+ Upala mu sjekira u med - His axe fell into honey \(Sudden and unexpected stroke of good luck\).
+ Uzdaj se u se i u svoje kljuse - Trust in yourself and in your own horse.
+ Vidjet ćemo, rekli su slijepci - We shall see, said the blind \(Discussing the unknown \/ Blind leading the blind\).
+ Vrijeme će pokazati svoje - Time will show its own \(Only time will tell\).
+ Vrijeme je novac - Time is money.
+ Vuk dlaku mijenja, ali čud nikada - Wolf changes its hair coat, but never his character \(A leopard can’t change its spots\).
+ Za dobrim konjem, prašina se diže - Dust rises behind a good horse \(Attracting a lot of attention for a good reason\).
+ Zlatna sredina - Golden middle \(The golden mean \/ Similar to the Goldilocks story, referring to something that is just right or fine\).
+ Zrno po zrno pogača, kamen po kamen palača - Grain by grain \[makes\] bread, stone by stone \[makes\] a palace \(Many a little makes a mickle\).
+ Željezo se kuje dok je vruće - Iron is forged while it’s hot \(Strike while the iron is hot\).
+ Živi bili pa vidjeli - Stay alive and we\'ll see \(All will be revealed in due time\).
+ Malo sutra - \(When pigs fly\)\(Šefik in Banja Luka says this all the time\)
]
#block(above: 1.05em, below: 0.42em)[#text(size: 13pt, weight: "bold")[Everyday expressions you\'ll hear constantly#degmark ]]
#emph[\(Added below — these aren\'t proverbs, they\'re the small conversational glue that holds everyday Serbian\/Croatian\/Bosnian together. You won\'t find most of these in a dictionary, but you\'ll hear them a dozen times a day. Same double-gloss format as above: literal \/ what it actually means.\)]

#block(above: 0.42em, below: 0.5em)[
+ Zdravo - health\/hello#degmark 
+ Ćao - \(borrowed from Italian \"ciao\"\)\/hi or bye, informal#degmark 
+ Bok - \(archaic \"God\" greeting, still used in Croatian\)\/hi or bye#degmark 
+ Vidimo se - we see each other\/see you later#degmark 
+ Laku noć - light night\/good night#degmark 
+ Prijatno - pleasant\/enjoy, said when leaving a shop, a table, or hanging up on someone politely#degmark 
+ Nema na čemu - there\'s nothing on which\/you\'re welcome#degmark 
+ Nema problema - there\'s no problem\/no problem, don\'t worry about it#degmark 
+ Polako - slowly\/take it easy, no rush, calm down#degmark 
+ Ma daj - oh, give\/come on, no way, are you kidding me#degmark 
+ Ma nemoj - oh, don\'t\/you don\'t say, seriously?#degmark 
+ Ma idi - oh, go\/get out of here, no way \(disbelief\)#degmark 
+ Ma važi - oh, it\'s valid\/yeah sure, whatever you say \(sarcastic\)#degmark 
+ Svaka čast - every honor\/well done, respect, hats off to you#degmark 
+ Bujrum - \(Turkish loanword, \"please\/welcome\"\)\/help yourself, come on in, go ahead#degmark 
+ Izvoli \/ Izvolite - here you go\/please, go ahead, may I help you, here\'s your thing#degmark 
+ Živeli \/ Živjeli - long may they live\/cheers! \(toast before drinking\)#degmark 
+ Nazdravlje - to health\/cheers, or \"bless you\" after a sneeze#degmark 
+ Đe si \/ Šta ima - where are you \/ what is there\/what\'s up, how\'s it going#degmark 
+ Kako ide - how does it go\/how\'s it going#degmark 
+ Sve u redu - everything in order\/all good, all\'s well#degmark 
+ Ajde - come\/come on, let\'s go, alright then, hurry up#degmark 
+ Idemo - we go\/let\'s go#degmark 
+ Šta radiš - what are you doing\/what\'s up, whatcha up to#degmark 
+ Halo - hello\/how you answer the phone specifically \(not used as a regular greeting\)#degmark 
+ Ko je? - who is it?\/who\'s calling, who is this#degmark 
+ Zvaću te - I\'ll call you\/I\'ll call you#degmark 
+ Nazovi me - call me back\/call me#degmark 
+ Kasnije te zovem - I\'ll call you later\/talk to you later#degmark 
+ Ajmo na kafu - let\'s go for coffee\/let\'s grab a coffee, let\'s catch up#degmark 
+ Sedi, sedi - sit, sit\/come on in, stay a while \(hospitality — never turn down the coffee\)#degmark 
+ Časti me - treat me\/it\'s your treat, you\'re buying#degmark 
+ Ja častim - I\'m treating\/this one\'s on me#degmark 
+ Nije loše \/ Nije bed - it\'s not bad\/it\'s decent, not bad at all#degmark 
+ Fol\(irati\) - fake\/to pretend, to fake it, \"as if\"#degmark 
+ Šta je, bre - what is it, \"bro\"\/come on man, seriously \(mild exasperation, very Serbian\)#degmark 
+ Daj molim te - give, please\/oh please, come on now \(disbelief or annoyance\)#degmark 
+ Nije bitno - it\'s not important\/doesn\'t matter#degmark 
]
